From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:47:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: skip CRC on color targets the render pass loads

A CRC-enabled render target forces its preload frame shader to ALWAYS
mode (pan_fb.c), so a pass that loads a full-screen target reloads every
tile even when it draws to only a few. Hades' own Vulkan renderer does
~46 such LOAD/STORE passes per frame; PanVK shaded ~2.9x the fragments of
the Mali DDK, nearly all of them preload threads.

Don't select CRC for a color target that the pass loads from memory. Its
CRC is invalidated like any other unselected target and the preload stays
INTERSECT. Tiles a load pass doesn't draw to aren't written back anyway,
so transaction elimination saves little there.

Hades (Vulkan renderer), Mali-G615 MC6 pinned: 502 MHz 31.9 -> 48.2 fps
(DDK 58.4), 1255 MHz 64.0 -> 103.1 fps (DDK 132.2). Hades through DXVK
unchanged (99.0 / 98.5 fps at 502 MHz). 64 small LOAD passes on one
1280x720 target: 7.6 -> 3.0 ms. PanProbe 38/38.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: skip CRC on color targets a render pass loads, so their preload stays INTERSECT instead of reloading every tile
Upstream-commit: none (generic PanVK; upstream candidate)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none
Validation test: Hades Vulkan renderer 31.9 -> 48.2 fps at 502 MHz (DDK 58.4), 64.0 -> 103.1 at 1255 MHz (DDK 132.2); Hades DXVK unchanged; PanProbe 38/38; no GPU faults
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.c               |  2 +-
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.h               |  9 +++++++++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c | 10 ++++++++++
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.c b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.c
index 8fa4cac..ba8ec28 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.c
@@ -662,7 +662,7 @@ pan_fb_store_target_should_crc(const struct pan_fb_layout *fb,
                                const struct pan_fb_store_target *rt,
                                unsigned tile_size)
 {
-   if (!rt->store || rt->crc_header_addr == 0 ||
+   if (!rt->store || rt->crc_header_addr == 0 || rt->no_crc ||
        !GENX(pan_image_view_can_crc)(rt->iview, tile_size))
       return false;
 
diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.h b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.h
index f9383a0..52e2197 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_fb.h
@@ -410,6 +410,15 @@ struct pan_fb_store_target {
 
    /** GPU address of the CRC header for this store target */
    uint64_t crc_header_addr;
+
+   /** Don't use CRC (transaction elimination) for this target
+    *
+    * A CRC-enabled target forces its preload to ALWAYS mode, which reloads
+    * every tile even when only a few are drawn to.  Drivers can set this when
+    * the target is loaded from memory, where CRC saves little.  The CRC is
+    * then invalidated like for any other unselected target.
+    */
+   bool no_crc;
 };
 
 static inline struct pan_fb_store_target
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index deabfc7..33fcb5b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -195,12 +195,22 @@ render_state_set_color_attachment(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
          att->clearValue.color.uint32[3],
       },
    };
+   /* Preloading a CRC-enabled target has to touch every tile (ALWAYS mode),
+    * while a pass that loads the target usually draws to only part of it and
+    * leaves the other tiles unwritten anyway. Skip CRC for such passes so the
+    * preload only runs on tiles that are drawn to.
+    */
+   const bool no_crc =
+      render->fb.load.rts[index].in_bounds_load == PAN_FB_LOAD_IMAGE;
+
    render->fb.spill.load.rts[index] = pan_fb_load_iview(&iview->pview);
    render->fb.spill.store.rts[index] = pan_fb_store_iview(&iview->pview);
+   render->fb.spill.store.rts[index].no_crc = no_crc;
    panvk_fb_store_set_crc_header_addr(&render->fb.spill.store.rts[index],
                                       iview);
    if (att->storeOp == VK_ATTACHMENT_STORE_OP_STORE && !ms2ss) {
       render->fb.store.rts[index] = pan_fb_store_iview(&iview->pview);
+      render->fb.store.rts[index].no_crc = no_crc;
       panvk_fb_store_set_crc_header_addr(&render->fb.store.rts[index], iview);
    }
 
